      "writtenOn": "2026-02-25T15:48:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`assembleExpression` can sometimes produce scratch let variables, although since this isn\u0027t overriding the mode, it will only happen if the expression has a child that would trigger it (e.g. in some matrix or function polyfill).\n\nThis puts the scratch let right before the for loop starts, which is fine so long as none of the variables in it reference the loop variable. A good test would be something like in SkSL:\n\n```\nfor (float a \u003d 12.0; a \u003e mod(sqrt(a), 5.0); a \u003d reflect(a, sqrt(a), 0.0)) {\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThis should produce extra statements for both `cond` and `nextExprs` to see how these get converted to wgsl.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2256,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2256,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "9bb87603d5c475e1603b03d5c1afa48d50c3d774",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c0773d3_49bb15fb",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLWGSLCodeGenerator.cpp",
